// SR 741.71 — Section 3 Collection and Payment of the Charge
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
Amended by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
|

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 6 Amount of the charge
The charge is CHF 40.
|

:INFO
Art. 6a Form of payment
The charge is payable:
a. by purchasing an adhesive vignette; or
b. by registering the vehicle registration plate in the information system of the Federal Office for Customs and Border Security (FOCBS) (e-vignette).
|

:NOTE
Art. 6a — Inserted by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
|

:INFO
Art. 7 Adhesive vignette
1 …
2 The adhesive vignette must be affixed directly to the vehicle before it is used on a Class I or II national highway for the first time in the period to which the charge applies.
3 It may only be transferred with the vehicle.
4 It shall be considered invalid if:
a. it is removed from the vehicle having been duly affixed; or
b. it is removed from the backing paper but not affixed directly to the vehicle.
5 The Federal Council shall regulate the affixing of the adhesive vignette.
|

:NOTE
Art. 7 — Amended by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
Para. 1 — Repealed by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, with effect from 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
Para. 5 — Inserted by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
|

:INFO
Art. 7a E-vignette
1 The vehicle registration plate must be registered before a Class I or II national highway is used for the first time in a period to which the charge applies.
2 The charge is deemed to have been paid for each vehicle that is lawfully permitted to be driven with the registered vehicle registration plate.
|

:NOTE
Art. 7a — Inserted by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
|

:INFO
Art. 7b Confirmation of authorisation to use Class I or II national highways
The person registering the vehicle registration plate may agree at the time of registration that confirmation that the charge has been paid be made publicly available in the information system.
|

:NOTE
Art. 7b — Inserted by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
|

:INFO
Art. 8 Period to which the charge applies
1 The charge applies for one calendar year. It is not refundable.
2 The vignette and the e-vignette entitle the holder to use Class I or II national highways from 1 December of the previous year until 31 January of the following year.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
|

:INFO
Art. 9 Issue of the adhesive vignette
The FOCBS issues the adhesive vignette.
|

:NOTE
Art. 9 — Amended by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).
|

:INFO
Art. 9a Collection of the charge
1 The following are responsible for collecting the charge in the form of an adhesive vignette:
a. the FOCBS, at the border;
b. the cantons, within the country.
2 The FOCBS is responsible for collecting the charge in the form of the e-vignette.
|

:NOTE
Art. 9a — Inserted by No I of the FA of 18 Dec. 2020, in force since 1 Aug. 2023 (AS 2023 337; BBl 2019 5889).

